cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this code or its results in published work, please cite the
  relevant version below AND the underlying physics references listed at
  the bottom. See docs/DATA_SOURCES.md for the full list of observational
  data sources used and how to cite them. v0.4-prelim+T75 (Tier-1
  milestone 2026-09-02: T72 DAMPE POC, T73 DAMPE CRE forward-model +
  joint-fit integration as Channel 17, T74 Zhang+2025 LSS / assembly-bias
  as Channel 18, T75 v0.7 full T41 rerun at nlive=500, T76 nlive=2000
  convergence check + doc-prominence fix; v0.7 result: log Z = -163.29
  +/- 0.085 (nlive=2000), tension T39 vs Yukawa a = 0.60 (below 1.0
  threshold), MAP m_chi = 770 GeV, sigma/m_0 = 0.27 cm^2/g; 472 tests
  passing). T77 (2026-09-02): defensive doc-update for the 2026-09-01 LZ
  mysterious signal (2.6sigma single event, implied WIMP mass >= 200
  GeV/c^2); per standing posture, sigma_DM-DM != sigma_DM-nucleon so LZ
  does not constrain sigma/m. T78 (2026-09-02): kinetic-mixing link
  refinement via Kahlhoefer et al. formula; at v0.7 MAP (epsilon ~ 10^-37,
  m_phi ~ 453 MeV) predicted sigma_DM-nuc ~ 10^-117 cm^2, suppressed by
  ~70 orders relative to LZ sensitivity (~10^-46 cm^2). T79
  (2026-09-02): composite form-factor F^2(q) correction (Gaussian + dipole)
  + relic-density consistency check (epsilon falls in freeze-in regime,
  consistent with T_RH > 10^15 GeV); uncertainty band updated to 50-80
  orders. T80 (2026-09-02): LZ paper preprint appeared (much earlier
  than the KIV cron's expected 2026-11-01 fire date); 25-page full
  author-list paper with 3.4sigma local / 2.6sigma global significance,
  best-fit Ls_10 WIMP at 1000 GeV/c^2; first compatibility check (NOT
  validation) of v0.7 posterior; project m_chi ~ 770 GeV in same
  ballpark as LZ best-fit. T81 (2026-09-02): defensive doc-update +
  Channel 19 added in response to LZ1.docx technical review of T80;
  reviewer's 5 recommendations all addressed: (1) cross-validation ->
  compatibility, (2) sigma/m survives all -> unchanged at current LZ
  precision, (3) T79 already executed (F^2(q) values documented), (4)
  LSS phenomenological status flagged prominently, (5) XENONnT
  (arXiv:2502.18005) + PandaX-4T (arXiv:2408.00664) watch registered
  as Channel 19 (experimental, not in primary production); 504 tests
  passing (was 472); 19 channels (was 18). Standing posture: LZ used
  as Channel 5 sanity check, NOT as sigma/m constraint. V0_6_ROADMAP: 9 of 15 items shipped across
  T71.2 -> T71.7 + 2 v0.4-prelim Tier-1 extensions (DAMPE, LSS). Earlier
  closed rounds: T71.4 (3 v0.6 items in parallel: hier-sparc +0.10 log Z,
  bullet_sens +1.74 log Z, CHANNEL_STATUS dict); T71.3 (R7 closure:
  nlive=2000 (Nc,Nf) scan via 7-way parallel background runner, scan
  converged); T71.2 (R16 closure: ksfr_mask_max_at_runtime field +
  config_hash field, 575/0/6 tests); T71.1 (R15 closure: inelastic +
  nlive=2000 + KSFR mask extension confound found). The KIV cron
  080d2f590251 (registered 2026-09-02) re-checks the LZ paper on
  2026-11-01 (60 days after the LZ announcement).
